### AI Code

AI Code is an AI assistant for creating and editing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript in uCoz templates. It takes into account template structure, system variables, conditions, and the specifics of uCoz modules.

AI Code can:

- find the right section of code in a template;
- apply changes directly in the editor;
- make targeted edits;
- create new blocks;
- create full landing pages;
- change HTML, CSS, and JavaScript;
- analyze template structure;
- work with module templates, global blocks, stylesheets, and personal pages.

AI Code supports two modes:

- **Autopilot** — automatic changes based on the request;
- **Manual mode** — review proposed changes and apply or discard them.

AI Code also works with visual references. A user can upload an image or screenshot from a computer, paste it from the clipboard, drag it into the interface, or choose it through the file manager.

AI Code can analyze the style and composition of an image, create similar blocks, fix visual issues, and use uploaded images in sliders, banners, and other site elements.

Create a backup before substantial template changes. In manual mode, changes can be reviewed before they are applied.

AI Code works inside the uCoz control panel. It is different from MCP: MCP connects external AI agents and IDEs to the site through the Model Context Protocol.

### AI content generation

AI content generation helps create new materials, update existing publications, prepare SEO data, and add images.

Supported modules:

- **Site News** — creating news, updating existing materials, and SEO optimization.
- **Blog** — automatic article generation from keywords and topics, SEO optimization, and image selection.
- **Article Catalog** — creating and updating articles, and optimizing materials for SEO.
- **File Catalog** — creating and updating file descriptions, and SEO optimization.
- **Ad Board** — creating and updating sales copy for listings, and SEO optimization.

AI can automatically create and edit:

- titles;
- body text;
- descriptions;
- tags;
- SEO titles and meta descriptions;
- covers and illustrations;
- other material fields.

Quick actions are available:

- rephrasing text;
- shortening;
- expanding;
- fixing grammar;
- updating individual parts of a material;
- undoing changes.

Web search mode helps use current data from open sources when preparing news and analytical materials.

You can set a personal style for text and image generation with custom instructions. This keeps a consistent brand tone, publication format, and editorial requirements.

AI helps prepare a material, but the user should check facts, style, images, SEO data, and the final version before publishing.

### uCoz MCP

[uCoz MCP](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/mcp) connects uCoz sites to external AI agents and IDEs that support the Model Context Protocol.

MCP lets you manage a site through a regular chat in Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, and other MCP clients.

Through MCP, an AI agent can work with the following areas:

#### Pages and templates

- creating and editing pages;
- creating and changing templates;
- managing menus;
- working with global blocks;
- setting up mail forms;
- checking code;
- creating backups;
- applying changes safely.

#### Site content

MCP supports work with:

- site news;
- the blog;
- the article catalog;
- the file catalog;
- the site catalog;
- the ad board;
- photo albums;
- video;
- FAQ;
- the forum;
- the guestbook;
- mini-chat;
- polls;
- categories;
- comments.

An AI agent can create, update, find, sort, and analyze site materials.

#### Online store

MCP lets you manage:

- categories;
- products;
- images;
- product variants;
- prices;
- stock;
- the cart;
- orders;
- order statuses;
- currencies;
- balance;
- product reviews.

#### Users and access

An AI agent can:

- view users and profiles;
- work with groups;
- manage ranks;
- view and change access rights;
- change a user's login, password, and group with confirmation.

#### Site files

MCP supports file operations over FTP:

- browsing files and folders;
- reading files;
- uploading files;
- creating folders;
- renaming resources;
- deleting files;
- getting public paths;
- managing FTP access.

#### Modules and settings

An AI agent can:

- view the module list;
- check module status;
- install and remove modules;
- enable modules;
- configure access through uAPI;
- check and manage site quarantine.

#### Server scripts

uCoz can provision an additional server environment for the site — a separate DirectAdmin environment next to the site, not a new panel module. Available both in the control panel and through MCP. In this environment you can publish and run custom PHP, Node.js, or Python code, set up a dedicated database for it, schedule regular runs, and back it up.

Through MCP an AI agent can:

- check the environment's readiness and enable it if needed;
- publish PHP code, and Node.js or Python apps with their own public URL in the form `https://{site}/apps{path}`;
- create a dedicated MySQL database with a user for the app;
- configure cron jobs to run scripts on a schedule;
- create and publish backups of the environment;
- export and import a database dump through phpMyAdmin.

#### Plans and subscriptions

MCP supports work with:

- pricing plans;
- subscribers;
- trial periods;
- access checks;
- subscription renewals;
- pausing subscriptions;
- canceling subscriptions;
- payments;
- refunds.

#### Whole-site design

The site design management tool lets you:

- check the site framework against uCoz rules;
- create templates;
- create global blocks;
- create informers;
- create standard pages;
- update the design of the whole site;
- check the project before publishing;
- manage saving and publishing changes.

#### AI skills

MCP can select, install, and run ready-made skills for specific tasks: creating landing pages, setting up a site, working with an online store, translating content, and editing design.

#### API reference

MCP can look up methods, parameters, and schemas in the official uAPI documentation and load the data needed to run requests accurately.

uCoz MCP can be connected in two ways:

- through the npm package `ucoz-mcp`;
- through the HTTP server `https://ucoz.com/mcp`.

A connection may require a uAPI token, the site URL, and FTP access, depending on the tools in use.

AI Code works inside the uCoz control panel, while MCP is used in external IDEs and AI agents. Access is controlled with a uAPI token and the permissions assigned to the site.

Do not publish tokens, passwords, or FTP credentials in code, chats, or public repositories. Before applying important changes, create backups and check the result.

## MCP skills

MCP skills are ready-made scenarios for AI agents. They contain instructions and proven action sequences for specific tasks on uCoz sites.

The catalog is intended for Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, and other AI tools that support MCP and skills.

### uCoz Landing Skill

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-landing-skill)

Creates and edits landing pages through MCP. The agent builds the page structure, adds a menu, forms, SEO markup, and a responsive design, uploads files, and changes uCoz templates.

### uCoz Provisioning Skill

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-provisioning-skill)

Creates a new uCoz site or connects an existing one, enables the required modules, configures uAPI, FTP, and MCP, and prepares the environment for further site management through an AI agent.

### Ad Campaign Landing Skill

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-ad-campaign-skill)

Creates separate landing pages for ads and audience segments, builds UTM links, and helps prepare campaigns for Yandex Direct and Google Ads.

### uCoz Shop Optimizer Skill

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-shop-optimizer-skill)

Audits an online store, improves categories and product cards, and helps with descriptions, images, and SEO. Price, stock, and order changes are not made without the user's confirmation.

### uCoz Site Translator Skill

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-site-translator-skill)

Translates and localizes site materials, templates, menus, and pages. It can translate content on the current site or create a localized version on another uCoz site, with a preview of the changes.

### uCoz Design Editor Skill

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-design-editor-skill)

Helps improve the site design. It edits templates, pages, CSS, the header, and the footer, and brings the look of different modules to one visual style.

### uCoz Template Creator

[Official skill](https://www.ucoz.com/ai/skills/ucoz-template-creator-skill)

Creates a custom site template with one design across sections, a responsive mobile version, clear navigation, content pages, and SEO markup.

